---
code: cmdsub-inner-nonleaf
when-fires: an effect-bearing command runs inside a `$(…)` substitution body, so it has no independent leaf. effect.rs classify (né dq-cmdsub-inner-nonleaf).
why: q-1.f silent-1/silent-4 disclosure; the inner command runs whenever its enclosing line runs. `{inner}` = the resolved inner argv.
edit-loop: edit a sentence in the transcript below, then run `mise run loom:compile -- cmdsub-inner-nonleaf && mise run loom:promote -- cmdsub-inner-nonleaf`; prove it stuck with `mise run test`, which is also what catches anything else the promotion moved. `mise run loom:vars -- --all cmdsub-inner-nonleaf` lists this case's values; type {{name}} to insert or move one.
---
-- book.sh --
#!/bin/sh
# `id -u` has no leaf of its own: it is part of evaluating the assignment.
uid=$(id -u)
hork --owner "$uid"

-- replay --
$ dorc plan --book=book.sh
note[cmdsub-inner-nonleaf]: Dorc cannot elide `id -u` on its own: it runs inside
a `$(...)` substitution as part of evaluating its enclosing line, so it runs
whenever that line does.
      [ book.sh:1:1
   1 | #!/bin/sh
     | \___/
